# Read from the root of the build context, which is the repository root: the agent's image is built
# with `-f packages/agent/Dockerfile .` because it shares `@sh/core` with the app. A .dockerignore
# next to that Dockerfile would not be read, and everything below would reach the image.

# Secrets. `packages/agent/.env` is the one the agent's own README tells an operator to create, and
# `COPY packages/agent` would otherwise bake a signing key into a distributable image.
**/.env
**/.env.local
packages/nextjs/setup-state.json
chain-signer.json

# Dependencies and build output: the image runs `yarn install` itself.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/artifacts
**/cache
**/typechain-types
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# History and local tooling, none of which the build reads.
.git
.github
.harness/runs
.harness/runtime
.harness/cache
**/.DS_Store
